    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0848" n="1806" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1806"/>

                <head>No. 40.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Lionel</hi>: In regard to the inquiry
                    contained in your note of the 25th instant, relating to the British vessels
                    seized in Behring’s Sea, I should be glad to have an interview with you this
                    afternoon at 3 o’clock, should that hour be convenient for you to come to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
